>So Mike the foretold Barbarian rushes up in the "y" direction to get near
>a Yeeghnho(sp?) that i hadn't tamed yet... in the process the said Demon Lord
>got in the way... i was just rushing in that direction and was still
>hitting "y" when it said REALLY attack the Yeeghnho? (y/n)? 

You know, I've been sitting here reading all the follow-ups to this post, and
a lot of them have good ideas/suggestions/etc. for how to modify the game to
prevent this kind of a problem.  The problem is, everything I've seen so far
makes the game more complicated!

As far as I see it, the easiest way to fix this problem is to simply require 
the user to hit [ENTER] after they type their answer.  This could be expanded 
to all y/n questions, to prevent the same problem from occuring in other 
areas.  Also, for those who might not want to take the time to hit [ENTER] 
after typing 'y' or 'n,' the game could still support the space bar as a 
default of 'y', without requiring you to hit the [ENTER] key after pressing 
it.

Comments?

